  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Polio Eradication Initiative Core Contributions for Financial Years 2022-23 to 2026-27</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment provides core funding to the World Health Organization for the Global Polio Eradication Initiative (GPEI). Australia&apos;s contribution will provide funding and technical assistance for polio surveillance, monitoring, supplementary immunisation campaigns and outbreak responses. It will help strengthen health and routine immunisation systems and ensure they are sustainably financed and managed. The total value of this investment is $36.05 million over five years, starting 2022-2023. It is the second phase of GPEI funding , following on from investment INL872 Polio and Routine Immunization 2015-2022.</narrative>
  </description>
